From: Ravindra Lakkireddy <85186928+rlakki08@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 03:41:57 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] fix: open checkout for "buy it" / "check out" / "pay for
 it" instead of starting a new search

Integration finding #10: with a hinge selected and placed, "buy it from the recommended seller"
and "check out with the recommended seller" both came back as "Searching the supply shops." +
search_started -- no fast path for checkout, and find_part's "Find a real part to buy" pulled
them in.

- fast path `_CHECKOUT_RE`: buy/purchase/order + it/this/that/these/those/them, pay for it /
  pay now / pay with ..., and "check out" on its own or before with/from/now/at/using ("check out
  this hinge" and "buy a hinge" still go to the LLM) -> start_checkout, no LLM call
- start_checkout now runs server-side: needs a selected part with sellers; seller_index null =
  a seller named in the command, else the cheapest/fastest if asked, else recommended_seller;
  the reply names the seller
- find_part's description no longer says "to buy"; start_checkout's says buy/check out/pay and
  takes a nullable seller_index

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
